Using Python
1: Two Sum

Brute Force Solution: 0(n^2) : Not Optimal Solution
The brute force loops are "looking forward" into the future. That's inefficient because you keep re-checking the same numbers.

class Solution(object):
    def twoSum(self, nums, target):
        for i in range(len(nums)):          
            for j in range(i + 1, len(nums)): 
                if nums[i] + nums[j] == target:  
                    return [i, j]
        return [] 

